    rheumatoid arthritis     n   71   mean T -1.259   T<=-2.5   5 (7.0%)
    no rheumatoid arthritis  n  917   mean T -1.167   T<=-2.5  67 (7.3%)
    excluded for unrecorded arthritis type: 123

  Arm F — PHQ-9 as a binary. A SUBSTITUTION for the continuous score, never
  an addition: the two are the same information and would collide.
  F: PHQ-9 >= 10 (substitution)  n 1,110  events  644  base 0.759 -> arm 0.758  delta -0.001 [-0.002, +0.000]  no detectable gain

  Arm I — physical activity: log MET-min/week (specialist references) plus
  sedentary minutes. 2005_2006 has no GPAQ items and is excluded from this arm
  rather than imputed; base and arm are refit on the same 2007+ women.
  I: physical activity (MET + sedentary) n   932  events  550  base 0.754 -> arm 0.753  delta -0.001 [-0.010, +0.007]  no detectable gain

  Arm G — diabetes. The diabetic bone paradox means type 2 diabetes raises
  measured BMD while also raising fracture risk, so a protective coefficient
  here is expected and is NOT evidence the model is wrong. There is
  deliberately no EXPECTED_SIGNS entry for it. Two reclassifications:
    G1: borderline coded as diabetic       AUC 0.755  (shipped 0.754, delta +0.001)
    G2: diabetes dropped entirely          AUC 0.754  (shipped 0.754, delta +0.000)

  Arm H — site sensitivity. The headline uses the WHO/ISCD lowest-of-two
  rule. These refit on each site alone to show the rule is not driving the
  result. Reported for the headline target only, and never re-ablated.
    H1: femoral neck only      n 1,111  events  618  AUC 0.745  (Ridge -> t_score)
